---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ExamShell from "../../../components/ExamShell.astro";
import ExamPractice from "../../../components/ExamPractice.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="TCF IRN for residence and nationality: practice mock – icanspeak French"
  description="The TCF IRN on the path to a French residence card or French nationality: what it is and free practice with our own mock and a reading test. General orientation, not legal advice."
>
  <ExamShell
    bild="dtz"
    header="TCF IRN for residence and nationality"
    title="TCF IRN for residence and nationality"
    titleKey="dtz.title"
    lead="France asks for a proven level of French at each step: for a first multi-year card, a first resident card and naturalisation (to verify). The TCF IRN is the test made for this. Here you can read about it and practise with our own mock."
    leadKey="dtz.lead"
    badges={["A2–B2"]}
    practiceHeading="Practise for the TCF IRN"
    practiceHeadingKey="dtz.practiceHeading"
  >
    <Fragment slot="info">
      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="dtz.who.title">Who is this for?</h2>
        <div class="exam-meta-row">
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="dtz.who.badge.result">Levels A2 to B2</span>
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="dtz.who.badge.course">For residence and nationality</span>
        </div>
        <p data-i18n="dtz.who.text">The TCF IRN (Test de connaissance du français pour l'intégration, la résidence et la nationalité) is run by France Éducation international and taken at approved centres. As far as we could check, it can be used to show the French level asked for a residence card or for naturalisation, and the level you need depends on the step: A2, B1 or B2 (to verify). Some people are exempt, and other tests or diplomas may count instead. The rules change, so check the official sources before you book. This is general orientation, not legal advice. We are not affiliated with France Éducation international.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="exam.skills.title">Skills tested</h2>
        <div class="skill-grid">
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">📖</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.lesen">Lesen</h4><p data-i18n="skill.lesen.desc">Leseverstehen</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🎧</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.hoeren">Hören</h4><p data-i18n="skill.hoeren.desc">Hörverstehen</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">✍️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.schreiben">Schreiben</h4><p data-i18n="dtz.skill.schreiben.desc">Written tasks</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🗣️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.sprechen">Sprechen</h4><p data-i18n="skill.sprechen.oralDesc">Spoken expression</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="dtz.format.title">How our mock is built</h2>
        <div class="format-table-wrap">
          <table class="format-table">
            <thead><tr><th data-i18n="format.th.part">Part</th><th data-i18n="format.th.what">What it tests</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen1.part">Listening: messages and radio</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen1.what">Short announcements, phone messages and radio items, with one question each</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen2.part">Listening: conversations and opinions</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen2.what">Everyday conversations with two tasks each; three people matched to what they think</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read1.part">Reading: contents page and adverts</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read1.what">Find the right chapter in a guide; match situations to adverts</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read2.part">Reading: short texts and rules</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read2.what">An email, a forum, local news and a set of rules or a contract</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read3.part">Reading: an email with gaps</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read3.what">Choose the word that fits each gap</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.write.part">Writing</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.write.what">One message or email from a choice of two, with a model answer and a checklist</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="format-note" data-i18n-html="dtz.format.note">This is the structure of our own mock, not of the real TCF IRN: the real test has its own parts, number of questions and timings, which we have not copied and which are to verify on the official site. See also our <a href="/tcf">TCF overview</a>. The mock has no speaking part: practise that with our <a href="/expression-orale/serie/a2-en-ville">speaking tasks</a>. The extra <a href="/lecture-ecriture">reading &amp; writing</a> tasks are good for more practice.</p>

        <h3 data-i18n="dtz.scoring.title">How the TCF IRN reports your result</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="dtz.scoring.text">As far as we could check, the TCF IRN gives you a level on the European scale (CEFR) for each skill, and the certificate is valid for a limited time (to verify the exact rules). In our mock the point bands are <strong>our own guide</strong>, not a TCF score or level.</p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <div class="mock-cta mock-cta--lead">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.set.title">Our TCF IRN mock: listening, reading and writing</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.set.text">Nine parts, 45 scored tasks in French between A2 and B1 (set 1) and B1 and B2 (set 2): listening parts 1–4 and reading parts 1–5, plus a writing task with a model answer. You can run a clock for each skill. At the end you see your result by part, with our own point bands as a guide. Progress stays saved in the browser.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/residence-et-nationalite/tcf-irn/serie-d-entrainement" data-i18n="exam.startSet">Start the practice set</a>
      <a class="plan-link" href="/plan-d-examen" data-i18n="plan.link">Your plan up to the exam →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.path.title">The whole path to residence and nationality</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.path.text">Which level and which civic exam each step asks for, who may be exempt and the order of the steps to naturalisation.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/residence-et-nationalite" data-i18n="dtz.path.cta">See the path</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.mock.title">Shorter: mock reading test (tasks 1–4)</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.mock.text">All four reading tasks as one continuous test at level B1, with an overall result at the end.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/residence-et-nationalite/tcf-irn/examen-blanc" data-i18n="dtz.mock.start">Start the mock test</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="fallen.title">Exam traps</h2>
      <p data-i18n="fallen.entry.blurb">Spots with a catch – briefly explained, with an example and a task to try.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/examens/pieges" data-i18n="fallen.entry.cta">See the traps</a>
    </div>

    <ExamPractice
      heading="Train the basics"
      headingKey="exam.practice.heading"
      intro="These practice tools train the skills that the TCF IRN tests."
      introKey="dtz.practice.intro"
      tools={["artikel", "grammatik", "wortschatz", "sprechen", "lesen"]}
    />
  </ExamShell>
</Layout>
